# Example .dockerignore for the kardamom workspace root.
#
# A .dockerignore MUST live at the build context root (= the repo root) to take
# effect; it cannot live under deploy/cluster/docker/. Copy this file there:
#
#     cp deploy/cluster/docker/dockerignore.example .dockerignore
#
# It keeps large, build-irrelevant trees out of the context sent to the Docker
# daemon for `service.Dockerfile` (which uses the repo root as context),
# dramatically shrinking the upload and speeding up builds. The cargo build
# inside the image regenerates target/ via BuildKit cache mounts, so excluding
# the host target/ here is safe (and important — it can be many GB).

# Rust build output (rebuilt inside the image)
target/

# Git metadata (not needed for the build)
.git/
.gitignore

# Claude / agent workspace + worktrees (not part of the build)
.claude/

# The cluster deployment tree itself — Dockerfiles are passed via -f, none of
# the Vagrant/Ansible/Nomad assets are needed inside the build context.
deploy/cluster/

# Editor/OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
